# Line endings are decided here rather than by whoever happens to clone.
#
# Without a global rule the answer comes from each machine's core.autocrlf,
# which is true on a Windows install and false on CI. The cost is not tidiness:
# a Go file checked out with CRLF makes `gofmt -l .` list nearly every file in
# the repository — 312 of 483 before this — so the one local check that would
# catch real formatting drift is drowned, and the offender is found by CI going
# red instead.
#
# This rule is first on purpose. Later rules win in a .gitattributes, so every
# specific declaration below still overrides it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts, where LF makes a batch file misbehave in ways that look
# like the script being wrong.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Declared binary rather than left to `text=auto` detection, because for these
# a wrong guess corrupts the file instead of formatting it oddly.
#
# The .wasm entries are the ones that matter most. A plugin bundle's identity is
# a SHA-256 over its manifest and module (ADR 0021), and its signature is
# checked before it is ever compiled — so a single byte changed by line-ending
# conversion does not produce a subtly wrong plugin, it produces one that no
# longer verifies. The .syso files are COFF objects the linker reads byte for
# byte, and the installer bitmap likewise.
*.wasm binary
*.syso binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.bmp binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3 binary
*.flac binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.onnx binary

# The embedded client bundle is a generated build artifact (committed so
# `go build` is self-contained). Keep it out of general line-ending churn, but
# pin its text files to LF so a Windows build and a Linux CI build produce
# byte-identical output — Vite emits LF everywhere except index.html, whose
# endings otherwise diverge by platform and break the CI drift check.
internal/web/dist/** -text
internal/web/dist/index.html text eol=lf
internal/web/dist/assets/*.js text eol=lf
internal/web/dist/assets/*.css text eol=lf

# The HTML template Vite passes through to dist/index.html: keep it LF so the
# generated file's endings don't diverge by build platform.
web/index.html text eol=lf

# Brand source art — binary, never normalized.
assets/** binary
